It's not clear to me there is a bug. From my reading, syncPod and syncBatch->syncPod appear to be called in mutually exclusive ways:

```
	// syncPod and syncBatch share the same go routine to avoid sync races.
	go wait.Forever(func() {
		select {
		case syncRequest := <-m.podStatusChannel:
			klog.V(5).Infof("Status Manager: syncing pod: %q, with status: (%d, %v) from podStatusChannel",
				syncRequest.podUID, syncRequest.status.version, syncRequest.status.status)
			m.syncPod(syncRequest.podUID, syncRequest.status)
		case <-syncTicker:
			m.syncBatch()
		}
	}, 0)
```

If there is a bug, can you demonstrate that with a test before changing this and adding locks?
